From: Kevin Finisterre <kfinisterre@KevinsMacStudio.localdomain>
Subject: [PATCH] rtlsdr_set_sample_slew: the sample clock a fraction of a ppm off, while streaming

The RTL2832U's sample frequency correction (demod page 1, 0x3e-0x3f) has
steps of 2^-24, about 0.06 ppm; the library only ever sets it to a whole
ppm, with the frequency correction. New call rtlsdr_set_sample_slew(dev,
ppm) sets it to the device's correction plus any ppm, at once and without
the demodulator reset a new sample rate takes. Receivers on one clock (a
KrakenSDR's five) are lined up by it to a fraction of a sample: one stick
run fast or slow for a moment slides its samples against the others. The
default is unchanged. The register's meaning is the library's own; no code
taken from elsewhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/include/rtl-sdr.h b/include/rtl-sdr.h
--- a/include/rtl-sdr.h
+++ b/include/rtl-sdr.h
@@ -418,6 +418,19 @@
  */
 RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_set_dithering(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, int dither);
 
+/*!
+ * The sample clock this many ppm off the rate set (on top of the device's own
+ * correction, rtlsdr_set_freq_correction), in the RTL2832U's steps of 2^-24
+ * (0.06 ppm), while it streams: no reset, no gap. Receivers on one clock (a
+ * KrakenSDR) are lined up by it: a stick run 1 ppm fast for a second gains
+ * 1.024 samples at 1.024 MS/s on the others. 0 puts it back.
+ *
+ * \param dev the device handle given by rtlsdr_open()
+ * \param ppm the offset, -480 to 480
+ * \return -EINVAL out of range, -1 no device, 0 otherwise
+ */
+RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_set_sample_slew(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, double ppm);
+
 RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_check_dongle_model(void *dev, char *manufact_check, char *product_check);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
diff --git a/src/librtlsdr.c b/src/librtlsdr.c
--- a/src/librtlsdr.c
+++ b/src/librtlsdr.c
@@ -2180,4 +2180,22 @@
 		return -1;
 	r82xx_set_dither(&dev->r82xx_p, dither);
 	return dev->freq ? rtlsdr_set_center_freq(dev, dev->freq) : 0;
+}
+
+int rtlsdr_set_sample_slew(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, double ppm)
+{
+	int r = 0;
+	double v;
+	int32_t offs;
+
+	if (!dev)
+		return -1;
+	/* as rtlsdr_set_sample_freq_correction, finer than a whole ppm */
+	v = -(dev->corr + ppm) * TWO_POW(24) / 1000000.0;
+	offs = (int32_t)(v < 0 ? v - 0.5 : v + 0.5);
+	if (offs < -8192 || offs > 8191)	/* the register's 14 bits */
+		return -EINVAL;
+	r |= rtlsdr_demod_write_reg(dev, 1, 0x3f, offs & 0xff, 1);
+	r |= rtlsdr_demod_write_reg(dev, 1, 0x3e, (offs >> 8) & 0x3f, 1);
+	return r;
 }
